# Keep the build context small and keep host state out of the image.
#
# `data/`, `secrets/` and `.env` are real files on a workstation that publishes
# images, so none of them may ever be baked into a layer.
#
# `content/` is deliberately NOT excluded: dockge deploys a published image with no
# repo on the box, so posts have to be in the image or the blog is empty. Verified
# the hard way — with content/ ignored, a dockge-shaped run logged posts: 0 and
# served a feed with zero items.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data
secrets
*.local.md
test
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
README.md
RUNBOOK.md
.github
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
coverage
